{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.RadicalPairingIsSignRep","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.RadicalPairingIsSignRep","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.WritheMarkovInvariance"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.radical_pairing_ne_zero_of_sign_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.radical_pairing_ne_zero_of_sign_rep","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RadicalPairingIsSignRep.lean#L115-L129","doc":"**The obstruction is universal, not anchor-specific.**\n\nStated against the measured identity as a hypothesis (`hpair`: the radical\npairing of `nf β` equals the sign-rep value — verified to `1.3e-51` over\nthirteen words in `radical_pairing_sign_rep_probe.py`): the pairing is\nnonzero for EVERY braid word, so no braid's normal form is orthogonal to\nthe radical, so `G x = nf` is unsatisfiable for every braid.\n\nChoosing a different knot cannot rescue the demand. That is the fact that\nmakes re-solving it on the quotient and reporting an offset angle a\ncategory error rather than a numerical approximation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.signRepValue_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.signRepValue_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RadicalPairingIsSignRep.lean#L109-L113","doc":"**Never zero.** A `zpow` of a nonzero base is nonzero, for every exponent\nand hence every braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.signRepValue_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.signRepValue_inv","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RadicalPairingIsSignRep.lean#L97-L107","doc":"**Mirror sends it to its inverse.** From `writhe_inv`: the braid-word\ninverse negates writhe, so the sign-rep value inverts. This is the same\nmirror-oddness the framing prefactor carries — see\n`QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance`.\n\nNo `q ≠ 0` hypothesis: `zpow_neg` holds unconditionally in a field, so\nrequiring one would overstate what the statement needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.signRepValue_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.signRepValue_append","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RadicalPairingIsSignRep.lean#L89-L95","doc":"**Multiplicative over concatenation.** Immediate from `writhe_append`;\nthis is what makes the pairing a representation value rather than a\nword-dependent artefact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.signRepValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.signRepValue","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/RadicalPairingIsSignRep.lean#L81-L87","doc":"The value of a braid word in the **sign representation** of `H_n(q)`: the\none-dimensional representation sending every generator to `-q⁻¹`, which is\nthe antisymmetric eigenvalue of the Hecke relation\n`(σ - q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`. Graded by writhe, since each positive crossing\ncontributes one factor and each negative crossing its inverse. ","signatureChunk":0}]}